#====================================================================
# E249 — 未初始化所有权标志导致清理函数释放调用者栈对象
#====================================================================

id:                     E249
trigger_tool:           runtime
phase:                  runtime
error_signature:        Signal 11 \(core dumped\)|exit_code=139|AddressSanitizer: attempting free on address which was not malloc\(\)-ed
severity:               3
category:               c-ownership-uninitialized-state
match_keywords:         Signal 11, exit 139, attempting free, not malloc, shared ownership, stack object
title:                  未初始化所有权标志导致清理函数释放调用者栈对象
root_cause:             构造函数把调用者持有的对象指针交给子对象却未初始化 shared/owned 标志；清理函数读取不确定值并可能按独占所有权关闭后 free 该指针，造成 invalid free/SIGSEGV
affected_scope:         C/C++ 中以 shared/owned 标志决定嵌套对象所有权、且子对象或所有权字段未零初始化的运行时转换工具
verification_cmd:       用 ASan 运行触发子对象非空的官方输入，确认 bad-free 栈指向清理函数及调用者栈对象
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           initialize-borrowed-ownership
rec_description:        在构造共享子对象时明确设置 shared/borrowed 标志，并保持调用者作为唯一释放方；添加能走到该清理分支的确定性回归测试
rec_command:            track-edit add ${SOFTWARE} ${VERSION} ${SOURCE_FILE} && refresh-patch --auto ${SOFTWARE} ${VERSION}
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               manual-source-fix
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      zero-initialize-owner-struct
fallback_description:   若 API 约定允许，先整体零初始化结构体，再对借用指针显式设置 shared 标志
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:
forbid_1_pattern:       跳过核心转换|只测试.*help|忽略.*SIGSEGV
forbid_1_reason:        帮助路径不会触发对象所有权清理，无法证明核心转换可用
forbid_1_consequence:   包构建通过但官方数据转换仍在退出阶段崩溃
principles:
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []
doc_file:               doc/E249.md
last_updated:           2026-07-13
source_event:           fastga/1.5 FAtoGDB official HAP1.fasta.gz exit 139 on OpenHarmony aarch64
authors:                tianyi_wang <tianyiwang58@gmail.com>
source_pr:
source_commit:
metrics_success_count:  1
metrics_fail_count:     0
metrics_confidence:     1.0
metrics_last_used:      2026-07-13
